  "readyNote": "re-measured 11/10/2026 with the per-element probe (heading and text kinds added) on the published quickstart/ja-smallbiz/j6 1.0.1 (installer sha256 d1f755ea…; tasks/evidence/ds-remeasure-4-2026-10-11/ja-smallbiz-j6): first 4/12 — the accent-text, muted and body kinds sampled nothing (no #t3-mainbody or .t3-sl on the home page), the kept slideshow's 20 elements took the worn page's text colour, and the white 'Purchase Now' label on the accent panel read 1.94-2.56:1 under light accents. The kinds now read the whole wrapper, the slideshow's #333333 is given back (keepColors), the accent panel's text and outlined button take the accent's own text colour, and the dark logo is turned light under a dark system. Then 12/12 with Moxie, MotherDuck, Toggl Track and Apple, controls 0, kept bands 0 differences, no text under 4.5:1 worse than the template's own (lowest 4.53), 76% or more of the page follows, every contrast kind sampled in every view, dark and light screenshots looked at. Earlier: measured 10/10/2026 on ja-smallbiz/j6 1.0.1 (tasks/evidence/followups-2026-10-10/p6-dsdata/ready-templates.txt): 12/12, default unchanged, no text made less readable than the template's own under the systems tried, 76% or more of the page follows; its largest title is section-sized (no display heading on the home page), probed as a heading; no bare h2 display-size rule",
  "contrastNote": "re-measured 11/10/2026: the home page has no #t3-mainbody and no .t3-sl, so the first three kinds sampled nothing (the probe must find at least one element); they now read the whole wrapper: its links (accent-text), its paragraphs (muted, body) and list items (body); heading and text judge every visible heading and text element",
