  "followNote": "the 'Purchase Now' box is a .bg-primary panel (the accent fill) whose text and outlined button the template paints white in other rules: under a light accent (Moxie, MotherDuck, Toggl Track) the white label read 1.94-2.56:1; the panel's text takes the accent's own text colour (selectors.onAccent), its outlined button the same colour for label and line; 14/10/2026 (visual review, /index.php/home/car-services): that page wears the template’s red style, whose fills are literals the tokenized sheet does not reach — the featured “Service Pricing” card (.pricing-table .col-featured > .col: #db2d2e ground and 2px line, white price, 70% white lines, a white ghost “Book Your Service”) and the slider’s caption title boxes (.slider-content-inner .title h2, white on #db2d2e; found while checking) stayed red under every system. Both are the template’s accent fill: they take the system accent (!important, as the red style’s rules are more specific) and their words, lines and ghost button the accent’s own text. The other cards already follow the surface (their 1s transition is the template’s entrance animation) (the title’s rule is currentColor at the template’s 20%, sideRules). 15/10/2026: /index.php/home/car-services wears the red style, whose tokenized sheet paints the page (body, .container-lg) with --ds-c-surface (its page is white, the surface's colour) where the default style uses --ds-c-bg: under a system the page took the surface, not the page colour (#1a1a1a for #000000 under Moxie: the match check failed 8/9, desktop and phone, v9 inner page). The page and the boxed wrapper take the page colour, as on every other style; 19/10/2026 (probe v10): header, footer and main menu take the page ground (the template lifts them 1.00 off its white page; the surface made a block under Moxie and a grey ground behind the theme logos); the dark panels (.xblog leading article, login form, contact form, profile box: #1d1d1d with white words in the template) take the ink with on-ink words; module titles are ink chips, the hilite module the accent with accent-on words; nav carets, the slideshow ground, btn-inverse/btn-secondary words, btn-info, label-info (a neutral chip), panels (line rims, surface heads, fg titles), alerts (status fills, info on the surface), the colour swatches, the cancel button rim, the consent link hover and the field rims follow the system",
