  "contractNotes1317": "13/10/2026 (#1317): .has-bg (the slideshow) kept its #333 ground as a picture band; on a phone the slide photo does not cover it and 78% of the first screen stayed the template under Stripe. Worn as an ink band: the desktop photo still covers it, the phone shows the system ink. Second run: as an ink band its mixed-black ground read as the template own #1d1d1d on a phone (68% of the first screen under Stripe), so it is a brand band (the accent is never a template colour here); the slide box outline button takes the band words. 14/10/2026 (SCREEN-1 82%, Stripe at 390): the dark share of the first screen was not the slideshow photo (an img, masked) but the .bg-dark panel under the Logan photo (#1d1d1d, the template's own ink, white words), which a phone's first screen reaches; it and the info list's panel (the same class) are an ink fill now: under a light system their ground is the system's ink, under a dark one its surface, the white words kept.",
